  [Fun fact: The very first FORTRAN implementation was also written for the IBM 704 . ↩],
  [id="fn:nobody"\>],
  [When we say, Nobody wants to read code that looks like cons(1, cons(2, cons(3, cons(4, cons(5, null))))) , we mean it. Even the Lisp gurus of old didn’t want to deal with that, so in Lisp when you write '(1 2 3 4 5) , it is translated directly into a linked list of cons cells. ↩],
