  [David Wheeler is credited with what is often called The Fundamental Theorem of Software Engineering , “We can solve any problem by introducing an extra level of indirection.” The wording has evolved over time, and the corollary “…except for the problem of too many layers of indirection” is almost always quoted at the same time. ↩],
